make expects lines that tell Things To Do to begin with a tab.  The problem
is that the tabs originally in the makefiles distributed over the net
usually get expanded to spaces.  Thus nothing "appears" wrong, but make
isn't seeing its tabs.  

If you have the filter 'unexpand' available just rename the makefile to
something like xxxx and type:    cat xxxx | unexpand > Makefile
Then those lines with eight leading blanks will get their tabs back.

Barring that, just go into your favorite editor and change every instance
of eight blanks at the beginning of a line to a tab.  Everything should
still look the same.

Also, I have seen the above error message come about because somehow an
excessively long line in a makefile was folded (broken) into two lines.
Recognizing this might be a little tricky.  The solution is either
rejoining the lines or putting a backslash at the end of the first line.

If none of the above helps you'll just have to grab someone that
understands makefiles.  Or learn it yourself (it's not too bad).


